b). P(C = cIM = mo) = P(C = cIM = mt ) i.e. the probability of ciphertext c is equally likely for 2 different messages. 
c). The key is as long as the message and a key should be used uniquely with a probability 1/IKI where IKI is the key space. 
Pr[M=m;C=c]=Pr[M=m] 

A bit stream with maximum Shannon entropy (ergo maximum information content) is nature agreagted random noise. It contains the maximum possible “information content” in terms of bits needed to represent it, it is computationally incompressible, 
it also has no meaningful or useful information in the conventional sense. 

Claude Shannon proved that achieving information-theoretic perfect secrecy demands that every key bit of a secure bit stream is chosen uniformly at random, meaning the min-entropy per bit is maximal.
